<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-7085] When PDS is enabled and IGNITE_BINARY_SORT_OBJECT_FIELDS property is set and IgniteCache#put is called a node hangs</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7085</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When PDS is enabled and IGNITE_BINARY_SORT_OBJECT_FIELDS property is set and IgniteCache#put is called a node hangs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The root cause is that when IGNITE_BINARY_SORT_OBJECT_FIELDS flag is enabled&lt;br/&gt;
BinaryMetadata#fields field is stored as TreeMap, but because BinaryUtils#WRAP_TREES is&lt;br/&gt;
set by default, that leads to BinaryMetadata#fields being wrapped into a BinaryTreeMap.&lt;br/&gt;
When an update for BinaryMetadata is initiated it ends up in a discovery thread from where&lt;br/&gt;
a metadata update for BinaryTreeMap is initiated. Since this update should be processed by the same discovery thread, that results in a deadlock.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13122143">IGNITE-7085</key>
